 "text": "Hey, how are you doing? Sure. A complementary colour is one that gives the eye a rest when it's used opposite it on the spectrum. It gives your composition balance and stops the eye getting tired. If you use two bright colours next to each other, a calming compliment helps. Yes, exactly. Black is fine for shadows, but a calming complement gives your painting a smoother feel. You could go with a dark grey instead. It gives you the same shadows but without the bright spot.",
